  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Differentiated HIV Services for Key Populations in Malaysia - Malaysia (01-Jul-2025-30-Jun-2028)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaysia, HIV, Malaysian AIDS Council (MAC)This program has the following goals: Ending AIDS by 2030 (90% reduction of new HIV cases from 2010 based on AEM) TARGETS: &#xf0b7; 95% of key populations tested for HIV and know their results &#xf0b7; 95% of people with diagnosed HIV+ receive ART &#xf0b7; 95% of people on ART achieve viral suppression &#xf0b7; 90% of key populations are reached by combination prevention services. The objectives of this program are: To increase HIV prevention Uptake among Key Populations through Outreach and PrEP Programs and reach 20% of MSM and TG people..  To increase HIV Screening uptake among Key Populations through Community-Based Testing and HIV-Self Testing programs and distribute 60,000 HIVST kits</narrative>
  </description>
